uestion_type":"application","question":"For $f\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ with $f(x)=x^2$, which set is the range?","options":["$\\mathbb{R}$","$(-\\infty,0)$","$[0,+\\infty)$","$\\{0,1\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"615f2d16fefaf40f0d6650ec","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the range of $f(x) = x^2$ when the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$(-\\infty,0]$.","$\\mathbb{R}$.","$(0,+\\infty)$.","$[0,+\\infty)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a601d9e740339b21521792d","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the range of $f(x) = \\sin x$ when the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$[0,1]$.","$\\mathbb{R}$.","$[-1,1]$.","$(-1,1)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"469bfa15d1b35c3aef58f8cb","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is the range related to the codomain?","options":["The codomain is always a subset of the range.","The range is a subset of the codomain.","The range and codomain must always be equal.","The range is unrelated to the codomain."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c875392e823b3be5124697c4","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Can two different functions have the same range?","options":["Every function has range equal to its domain.","A range can never contain more than one value.","Different functions may share the same range.","The range is determined only by the function name."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f6a6c7dee8af3dd20f946ad1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f$ have domain $\\{-1,0,1\\}$ and be defined by $f(x) = x^2$. What is the range?","options":["$\\{-1,0,1\\}$.","$\\{0,1\\}$.","$[0,+\\infty)$.","$\\{1\\}$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2442d80ca13e73322f6a8d72","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be given by $f(x) = x^2+1$. Which set is its range?","options":["$[1,+\\infty)$.","$[0,+\\infty)$.","$\\mathbb{R}$.","$(-\\infty,1]$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"07dbc813ddd63b28d2139d23","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why can the codomain be larger than the range?","options":["Because the range contains all inputs.","The codomain can contain unattained values.","Because the range must always be empty.","Because the range always equals the domain."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0b5016055a00ed7e431406ab","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What information is essential when determining the range of a formula?","options":["Only the letter used for the dependent variable.","The domain of the function.","Only the name of the course.","Only whether the function has a graph."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6a2a44e8494aa79aa939ad35","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f$ have domain $[0,2]$ and be given by $f(x) = x^2$. What is the range?","options":["$[0,+\\infty)$.","$[0,4]$.","$[-4,4]$.","$[2,4]$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"86a1932ae0e765209005758a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_range_7d5f6aa1_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which two functions have the same range on the domain $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$f(x) = x$ and $g(x) = x^2$.","$f(x) = x^2$ and $g(x) = |x|$.","$f(x) = \\sin x$ and $g(x) = x$.","$f(x) = x^2+1$ and $g(x) = x^2$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d0da2e3a2a9d76989f8afc03","time_limit":40},{"id":"range_image_new_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A function is surjective exactly when its range equals which set?","options":["codomain","domain","graph","derivative"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1ef0b58b5e463863e830c6ed","time_limit":30},{"id":"range_image_new_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which variable is called dependent in $y=f(x)$?","options":["$x$","The domain","$y$","The codomain"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"67606803da895b71db6f6be5","time_limit":20},{"id":"range_image_new_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Restricting the domain of a function generally does what to its range?","options":["It can shrink the range","It always enlarges the range","It never changes the range","It empties the range"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4c5cde95df2b1911cee3a58f","time_limit":30},{"id":"range_image_new_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The range of $f\\colon X\\to Y$ is which set?","options":["$\\{f(x)\\colon x\\in X\\}$","$X$","$Y$","$\\{x\\colon f(x)=0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"716ae14e4b6220fd0a73d85c","time_limit":20},{"id":"range_image_new_017","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the range of $f(x)=\\sin x$ on $[0,\\pi]$?","options":["$[0,1]$","$[-1,1]$","$[-1,0]$","$\\{0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"04d387cfdedc52921811c373","time_limit":30},{"id":"range_image_new_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=x^2$ with domain $[-1,1]$. What is the range?","options":["$[0,